# init.recovery.vold_decrypt.rc
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (do not delete)
# -----------------------------------
# TWRP-11's system/etc/init/hw/init.rc contains:
#     import /init.recovery.vold_decrypt.rc
# A missing import target is a FATAL parse error in AOSP init -> init aborts ->
# kernel panic -> bootloader watchdog reset -> boot loop.
#
# The upstream body starts `vold` for metadata/FBE decryption. This device uses
# Qualcomm wrappedkey_v0 (TEE/keymaster backed), which TWRP cannot service, and
# system/bin/vold is not part of this minimal recovery ramdisk, so the file is
# intentionally empty.
#
# NOTE: BoardConfig.mk sets TW_INCLUDE_CRYPTO := true,
# TW_INCLUDE_CRYPTO_FBE := true and TW_INCLUDE_FBE_METADATA_DECRYPT := true.
# Those flags make TWRP *attempt* decrypt; they do NOT put vold in the ramdisk.
# If you ever want real vold-based decrypt, add the vold service (and binary)
# here. Until then, use "Format Data" / disable encryption from TWRP.
